# TITLE: Multicast & Special-Use IP Ranges
# DESCRIPTION: Rule set for blocking local-network multicast/broadcast and special-use IP ranges. Use with REJECT (for privacy) or DIRECT (if local discovery is needed). Compatible with Shadowrocket / Surge (RULE-SET format).
# UPDATED: 2026-11-04
# REPO: https://github.com/your-username/your-repo

# --- SSDP (UPnP) ---
# Smart TVs, speakers, Chromecast, etc.
IP-CIDR,239.255.255.250/32,no-resolve

# --- mDNS (Bonjour) ---
# Printer discovery, Apple TV, AirPlay, etc.
IP-CIDR,224.0.0.251/32,no-resolve

# --- Multicast Range ---
# Covers various local service discovery protocols
IP-CIDR,224.0.0.0/4,no-resolve

# --- Limited Broadcast Address ---
# Sends to all devices in the local network
IP-CIDR,255.255.255.255/32,no-resolve

# --- Subnet Broadcast Address (adjust to your subnet if needed) ---
# Prevents unnecessary gateway spam; update 192.168.1.255 to match your local network
IP-CIDR,192.168.1.255/32,no-resolve

# --- Documentation & Special-Use Ranges ---
# Should never route to the public internet
IP-CIDR,192.0.2.0/24,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,198.51.100.0/24,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,203.0.113.0/24,no-resolve
